# The Controller page with a virtual Xbox pad: its south button given Quick
# Save from the list, its north found by pressing it and given Quick Load;
# then a controller SDL has no mapping for, mapped by the wizard -- its face
# buttons pressed, the rest skipped -- and Play: test_ui_scripts.c reads
# User.ini, gamecontrollerdb.txt and what the engine got.
pad attach xbox
wait 1.5
expect home
find Settings
key Return
wait 0.5
expect settings
find Controller
key Return
wait 0.5
find A
key Return
wait 0.3
expect pick
find Quick Save
key Return
wait 0.3
expect settings
find Find a button
key Return
wait 0.3
pad button 3 down
wait 0.15
pad button 3 up
wait 0.3
key Return
wait 0.3
expect pick
find Quick Load
key Return
wait 0.3

# A second controller, SDL's none: chosen above the model, mapped from the
# rows' end.
pad attach raw
wait 0.5
find Controller
key Right
wait 0.3
find Layout
find Map this controller...
key Return
wait 0.5
expect padwizard
pad button 0 down
wait 0.15
pad button 0 up
wait 0.3
pad button 1 down
wait 0.15
pad button 1 up
wait 0.3
pad button 2 down
wait 0.15
pad button 2 up
wait 0.3
pad button 3 down
wait 0.15
pad button 3 up
wait 0.3
find Skip
key Return
wait 0.1
key Return
wait 0.1
key Return
wait 0.1
key Return
wait 0.1
key Return
wait 0.1
key Return
wait 0.1
key Return
wait 0.1
key Return
wait 0.1
key Return
wait 0.1
key Return
wait 0.1
key Return
wait 0.1
key Return
wait 0.1
key Return
wait 0.1
key Return
wait 0.1
key Return
wait 0.1
key Return
wait 0.1
key Return
wait 0.1
wait 0.3
expect settings
find Done
key Return
wait 0.5
expect home
find Play
key Return
wait 2.5
expect recovery
find Quit
key Return
